(6804046, 1021909, 108580, '<td valign="top">"A wildlife shot with artificial light."<br/>Fabulous work and spot-light as mentioned in my original comment. I voted an 8. <br/>However I contest this is not a wildlife shot. It is a nature image shot under controlled in captivity conditions and I feel very strongly about the distinct difference between the two. I have no problem with zoo or sanctuary images and encourage my photo students to visit them, support them, and practice technique there for the day that that elusive subject appears before them in the real wild. I just make sure they make that distinction if they publish their captivity photos.<br/>Again, a marvellous image and congrats on your HM!</td>', '"A wildlife shot with artificial light."Fabulous work and spot-light as mentioned in my original comment. I voted an 8. However I contest this is not a wildlife shot. It is a nature image shot under controlled in captivity conditions and I feel very strongly about the distinct difference between the two. I have no problem with zoo or sanctuary images and encourage my photo students to visit them, support them, and practice technique there for the day that that elusive subject appears before them in the real wild. I just make sure they make that distinction if they publish their captivity photos.Again, a marvellous image and congrats on your HM!', '2012-06-29 02:16:46.000000', NULL, 0),
